&lt;h2&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is a minor known regression with the Qt 6 based build of the app when&lt;br&gt;
running on Linux with Wayland. Reordering items via drag and drop works, but you&lt;br&gt;
sometimes have to click somewhere (for example, the tool bar) to re-enable&lt;br&gt;
hover for the items afterwards. This has been reported as a bug in Qt&#39;s&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-109826&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;bugtracker&lt;/a&gt;. Usually, you can&lt;br&gt;
start the app with the &lt;code&gt;-platform xcb&lt;/code&gt; option to force X11/XWayland, which does&lt;br&gt;
not show the same symptoms.&lt;/p&gt;
